en:
I can't stand it anymore.
I have to see someone fall from the roof.
And I want to know whether they survive!{p}

By the time Aizawa got there, a pool of blood had already spread far and wide around Kuwahata, who lay limp and motionless.
He watched him closely for a while, but there was no sign of movement.
When he touched him, the body had already gone cold.{p}

"...He's dead."
Aizawa smiled, satisfied.
Now he knew the result, and the weight on his heart was gone.{p}

But when three delinquents had killed themselves one after another, even the school couldn't keep quiet any longer.
Was a war breaking out between delinquents, or was some other problem at work? The police investigation grew more intense as well.
And as a first step, the roof was put off-limits.{p}

Once he'd called the friend out, he suddenly attacked from behind and made the friend breathe in chloroform.
Just like the first experiment, it worked without a hitch.
But now he had to haul this limp guinea pig all the way to the school roof.{p}

He felt as if he had become the king of this world.
He could end the life of any of those wretched humans he could see from this spot, any time he pleased.
The thought struck him as hilarious.{p}

Then, when they searched Aizawa's house, they found everything that had happened recorded in detail in his diary.
And, astonishingly, even the events of his final moments the night before, which he couldn't possibly have written.
It was written down as if he had foreseen how things would turn out.{p}

Naturally, neither the police nor the school believed that part.
Someone who threw himself off a roof couldn't possibly write down everything up to the very instant of his death.
The diary ended like this.{p}

Even now, everything is still shrouded in mystery.
And that's the end of my story.
Well then, I'll hand things over to the next person.{p}

Does this school hold some kind of secret, I wonder?
...We're getting close to the roof now.
Look, once we climb these stairs, the roof is right there.{p}

"It's Aizawa!
Look, it's Aizawa!"
Arai, who had been gripping the railing beside {f:me|me}, suddenly pointed into the empty air and climbed right over the top of it.{p}

And as he plunged toward the ground... he suddenly vanished{f:.|.}
It was as if his particles had come apart and melted straight into the air; he was gone without a trace{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} slowly looked up at the sky, stunned.{p}

Of course.
That's proof that you're normal, {a}{f:.|.}
Everyone has what they call an instinct for self-preservation, it seems...
But there was once someone who felt no fear at all, no matter how frightening the place.{p}

I see.
That's a serious matter, you know.
Well, I'll talk about that some other time.{p}

This is my chance, Morikawa thought.
He told the teacher he had a stomachache and sat out P.E.
For a while he lay in the nurse's office, but after about ten minutes he slipped out of bed and went back to the classroom.{p}

That's right, he threw it in the trash can.
Then he quietly went back to the nurse's office.
After fourth period ended, he waited a while, then went back to the classroom.{p}

When the teacher came in, the kids sitting around Nakayama whispered to cheer her up.
"Yoko, I'll help you look later."
"You'll find it."{p}

"Today, I'm going to kill something even more fun.
I'll tell you about it next time."
With that, she walked away.{p}

(Something more fun...?
What the hell is she planning to do★)
Morikawa stood frozen on the spot until she was out of sight.{p}

There was another noise.
(Maybe it's the neighbors' TV?)
That was how unreal it was: a violent noise, just like a sound effect.{p}

Just then, a scream suddenly came from inside.
"Mom★"
He flung the door open.{p}

Not long after that, Nakayama started coming to school again.
I heard all this when I went to visit Morikawa in the hospital.
To me, he didn't look like he was lying.
What do you think, {a}{f:?|?}
Do you believe what Morikawa said?{p}

...They say the killer still breaks into people's homes and commits murder.
You should be very careful to lock up at night too, {a}{f:.|.}{p}That's the end of my story.
Next, please.{p}

"So what? It's just a hamster.
Ugh, give me a break. People eat meat and fish without batting an eye, and then they get all sad when a pet dies? They've seen too many comics and movies."
Morikawa said that and didn't give it another thought.{p}

He walked on briskly for a while, but something nagged at him, and when he looked back, Nakayama was still standing there in a daze.
(What's with her?)
He must have been in a foul mood, so he decided to take a little detour.{p}

Why would Nakayama do something like that?
Morikawa couldn't understand it.
All he knew was that an indescribable unease was spreading through his heart.{p}

Thinking he was in trouble, Morikawa peeked out from behind the tank.
But there was no one there.
Relieved, he turned around, and...{p}

And then she sank her teeth into the side of his neck.
Nakayama tore off his flesh, one bite, then two.
And then, in unbearable agony, Morikawa climbed over the railing himself and jumped.{p}

He didn't survive.
He had his answer.
On the ground where he had jumped, a vivid bloodstain spread out.{p}

Should he push off a teacher he disliked, or else...
He couldn't decide.
So he decided to take his time and work out a plan up on the roof.{p}

Later, when we went up to the roof for science class, I thought I heard Aizawa's voice.
Several other students heard it too.
I wonder... did he die after all...?{p}

What about you?
Would you like to try...?{p}That's the end of my story.
Let's hear from the next person...{p}

But as he was about to head home, he found Kuwahata lying in wait for him at the school gate.
Aizawa did as Kuwahata told him and followed him up to the roof.
Kuwahata's revenge had begun.{p}

The next day, Aizawa lured a teacher up to the roof, saying that Kuwahata had pushed someone off.
"Where'd that Kuwahata go?"
Then the teacher leaned over the railing at the spot Aizawa pointed to and peered down.{p}

He decided not to push Kuwahata off.
Instead, he put his hands on the roof's railing and jumped down himself.
Leaving Kuwahata lying on the cold concrete of the roof...{p}

Aizawa's scream rang out.
And the answer had come.
Aizawa did not survive.{p}

This time too, he called out a delinquent, waited for an opening, and made him inhale chloroform he'd prepared in advance.
The delinquent went limp at once, without even a chance to resist.
Aizawa pushed him off, just as he had Kuwahata.{p}

He ran straight down the stairs to check.
The delinquent was dead.
"So Kuwahata must be dead too."{p}

The next day, the school was in an uproar.
The friend who had escaped from Aizawa had confessed everything.
All sorts of rumors spread around the school.{p}

But when they searched Aizawa's house, they found a diary recording everything that had happened in minute detail.
Astonishingly, it even described what happened in his final moments the day before, which he couldn't possibly have written.
As if he had foreseen that it would happen.{p}

"No... I'll pass."
{f:I|I} didn't have that kind of courage.
Who on earth was this Aizawa{f:?|?}
Hadn't he jumped{f:?|?}
And yet he was still turning up on the roof...
I felt that if I went up there now, something terrible would happen.
"Are you sure you don't want to go?"
Arai pressed me firmly.
{f:I|I} nodded silently and decided to hear the next person's story.{p}"Well then, let's move on..."{p}

...The next day, {f:I|I} told the club president what had happened and asked for the seven wonders feature to be cancelled.
The president had listened half in doubt at first, but on learning that the story of the vanished students was true, granted {f:my|my} request.
This was fine.
This was for the best{f:.|.}
Time passed, and {f:I|I} became a second-year.{p}

Another sharp pain shot through the back of my head.
...
Thinking of being pushed off the roof, {f:I|I} felt my consciousness slowly, quietly fade away...{p}
